 ## Background
-Deformable Neural Radiance Fields (Nerfies) was introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2021 [S1]. It builds on the original NeRF paper [39] by adding a continuous volumetric deformation field conditioned on per-frame latent codes. The method was motivated by the challenge of capturing people with hand-held cameras, where non-rigidity and camera motion make reconstruction difficult. It draws inspiration from geometry processing and physical simulation, specifically elastic energy formulations, to regularize the deformation field. The method was evaluated on data captured using a rig of two synchronized mobile phones [S1].
+Deformable Neural Radiance Fields (Nerfies) was introduced by Park et al. in 2021 [S2]. It builds on the original NeRF paper by adding a continuous volumetric deformation field conditioned on per-frame latent codes [S2]. The method was motivated by the challenge of capturing people with hand-held cameras, where non-rigidity and camera motion make reconstruction difficult [S2]. It draws inspiration from geometry processing and physical simulation, specifically elastic energy formulations, to regularize the deformation field [S2]. The method was evaluated on data captured using a rig of two synchronized mobile phones [S2].
 
